<title>UK: NWE vacuum gas oil steady but seen softening.</title>
<headline>NWE vacuum gas oil steady but seen softening.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>bid/ask	prev bid/ask</p>
<p> Low sulphur cargoes fob NWE	  125/127	  125/127</p>
<p> High sulphur cargoes fob NWE	 118/119	  117/118</p>
<p> High sulphur barges fob ARA	  121/122	  123/124</p>
<p> Formula quotation fob Med	     18/23	    18/23</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Euro VGO prices were steady to weaker on Friday with prices set to fall in the context of weak U.S. demand and expected over-supply, trader said.</p>
<p>The arb window to the U.S. remained shut and Russian VGO supplies were seen en route to pressure the market.</p>
<p>&quot;We are anticipating oversupply,&quot; said one trader. &quot;The buyers are holding off and are well-covered.&quot;</p>
<p>The next large cargo of low sulphur was seen out of Scandinavia loading around June 10th.</p>
<p>- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
